 2 Now playing   │ Getting started
 3 Streams       │ 
 4 Recognitions  │ · 1. Sign in  ✓ done
 5 Account       │      Sign in to your AudD account (or paste an API token) so audd can recognize music and show your
 6 Settings      │      account.
*7 Help          >      $ audd login --device
                 │ 
                 │   2. Recognize a file
                 │      Pick a file, URL, or folder and recognize it. Enter here fills in AudD's example song so you can
                 │      try a recognition.
                 │      $ audd recognize https://audd.tech/example.mp3
                 │ 
                 │   3. Use the microphone
                 │      In Recognize, open the Microphone tab to record a few seconds and identify the song.
                 │      $ audd listen
                 │ 
                 │   4. Add a stream
                 │      Have AudD monitor a radio or other live stream, then watch it in Now playing.
                 │      $ audd streams add <url> --id 1
                 │ 
                 │   5. Run any command
                 │      Press ctrl+k to search every command and run it from a form.
                 │      $ audd commands
                 │ 
                 │ Enter goes to the step. Every page shows the command it runs at the bottom; y copies it.
